  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday (Wednesday, post-Columbus Day) was structurally soft across the board, but Port Washington's performance masks a real operational concern that needs your attention today.\n\nPort Washington delivered $2,438 against a $3,408 comp \u2014 a 28% drop that looks worse than it is. Columbus Day landed two days prior, which typically depresses Wednesday revenue ~10%, and yesterday you ran 5 groomers vs. your trailing-30-day baseline of 5.6, which accounts for most of the miss. The real problem: $/groomer/day came in at $388 vs. your $467 baseline \u2014 your team is underproducing by roughly $80 per groomer. This isn't calendar noise; it's execution. Retail cratered 67%, which suggests front-of-house focus is down. Add-on attach actually improved to 50% (up from 41%), so upsell discipline is fine. Month-to-date Port is running 8.9% below DOW-adjusted expectation \u2014 that's real performance loss, not just calendar. Hicksville, by contrast, is tracking well: MTD up 12% and yesterday's $382/groomer nearly matches the baseline. You should be proud of that location's momentum and consistency.\n\nThe concerning pattern: both stores show a lapse pool (Port: 516 customers worth $318k annually; Hicksville: 193 worth $139k). That's reactivation fuel if you want it. Glen Cove remains a drag \u2014 0 groomers scheduled for today and tomorrow, 0 for the next 7 days. That's a decision point, not a data point.\n\nPort Washington today: 6 groomers, 15.0h bathers; tomorrow: 6 groomers, 15.0h bathers; next 7 days: 35 groomer-days total (up from MTD pace of 4.4/day)."
